! mcp_bootstrap_p44.strap -- THE CHARACTER LOCATOR TABLES and THE
! TABLES, printed page 44.  docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.51,
! header "PAGE NUMBER 44".  docs/boot_plan.md M3.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! FOUR STAND-INS LAND, ALL FOUR OF THEM printed p.43's
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! printed p.43 read four addresses off its own binary and wrote them
! as SYNs because the page that defines them had not been opened.
! This is that page, and it defines all four by name:
!
!   Q FLD   002456.00   line 4   -- p.43 line 46's LVE target
!   Q       002465.00   line 21  -- p.43 line 47's LF table
!   Q SAV   002472.00   line 28  -- p.43 lines 10 and 53's TI/SWAPI
!   Q TB    002500.00   line 30  -- p.43 line 26's LV
!
! Not one of them moves.  And the page's last datum ends at
! 002501.71, which docs/boot_plan.md A9 recorded as printed p.45's
! opening address before p.44 was rendered.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE NULL OPERATION FIELD, THIRTEEN TIMES
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Lines 4-16 have NOTHING in the operation column -- the statement
! begins with its comma.  C22-6531 printed p.7 calls that a NULL
! FIELD and strap_asm.py has compiled it since MCP printed p.25:
! what it lays down is the ADDRESS-AND-INDEX HALF WORD that every
! full-word format begins with, "ADDRESS(0-23) | 1000 | I(28-31)",
! and the listing prints the thirteen of them as 82 -- the 1000 and
! index $2.
!
! WHAT THE TABLE IS FOR is RefMan printed p.29, "Indirect
! Addressing": p.43 line 46's "LVE,$6,Q FLD($3)" fetches the half
! word at Q FLD+$3 and keeps chaining, and p.29 says the half word
! it lands on "is assumed to be either a half length instruction or
! the first half of a full length instruction ... No check is made
! for invalid operation codes."  So these thirteen rows are
! hand-built first halves whose only job is to carry a 6-bit-stepped
! address and the index $2.  The steps are 0, 6, 12, ... 72 -- one
! six-bit BCD character apiece, thirteen characters per zone, which
! is exactly the width of each of THE TABLES' four rows below.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! "UNTAIL" IS NEW AND IS THE OTHER HALF OF printed p.43's "TAIL,A"
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Line 35 is "UNTAIL,(1)".  C28-6129 printed p.38 (PDF 42):
!
!   "An untail statement will untail all levels up to and including
!    the level specified in the address field."
!
! and printed p.37 gives the level syntax, "TAIL, (n)DOG", with
! "(1)" the default.  SO MCP'S TAILING IS TWO LEVELS DEEP AND THEY
! NEST: printed p.2 line 10's "TAIL,(2)G" covers the whole program
! at level 2, printed p.43 line 9's "TAIL,A" opens level 1 over
! these two pages, and this line closes level 1 and leaves G
! standing.  Nothing before had shown the second level being used.
!
! IT IS DISCARDED FOR THE SAME REASON "TAIL" IS, and the reasoning
! is in strap_asm.py's LISTING_CONTROL note: tails mangle
! definitions and references alike, so a one-program assembly is
! bit-identical without them.  The condition that would make that
! wrong is a name used on both sides of a block boundary, and this
! page is where it could bite -- every symbol it defines lives
! inside the level-1 block.  tests/verify_mcp_bootstrap_p44.py
! CHECKS IT rather than asserting it.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE TABLES: FOUR ZONES OF THIRTEEN, AND THE COLON IS SPECIAL
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Lines 21-25 are the Hollerith-to-BCD output table, four rows of
! thirteen characters:
!
!   12 zone    A B C D E F G H I  +  .  )  /
!   11 zone    J K L M N O P Q R  -  $  *  /
!   zero zone  / S T U V W X Y Z  0  ,  (  :
!   no zone    1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8 9 (blank) = - /
!
! and Q TB's four VF values -- 0, 78, 156, 234 -- are those rows'
! bit offsets, thirteen characters times six bits apiece.
!
! THE ZERO ZONE IS WRITTEN IN TWO STATEMENTS because its thirteenth
! character is a COLON, which the 48-character set has no graphic
! for: line 23 stops after twelve and line 24 is
! "DD(BU,6,6),(8)32 -SPECIAL FOR COLON", the code written as an
! octal number.  printed p.42 line 35 put the same colon in an IQS
! table the same way, "(2)01110101", in binary there and in octal
! here.
!
! THE "0" IN THE ZERO ZONE IS A DIGIT, not a letter O, and the table
! settles it without a re-render: the tenth character of each row is
! that row's lone-zone punch -- "+" for 12, "-" for 11, blank for
! none -- so the zero zone's is the digit zero.  The "O" in
! "JKLMNOPQR" is a letter for the same structural reason.
!
! NO BINARY IS PRINTED FOR LINES 21, 22, 23 AND 25, so no character
! code on this page is checked or can be.  What IS checked is every
! row's LENGTH, by the address of the row after it, and the four of
! them together by Q SAV landing on 002472.00.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! SUBSTITUTIONS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! (1) BLANKS INSIDE SYMBOL NAMES ARE DROPPED, as on every page since
!     p.2: Q FLD, Q SAV and Q TB.  "Q" has no blank to drop.
!
! (2) "UNTAIL,(1)" IS WRITTEN AS PRINTED and the assembler discards
!     it, exactly as printed p.43 line 9's "TAIL,A" is.
!
! (3) NOTHING ELSE.  The two CNOPs, the null operations, the four
!     entry-mode DDs and the octal colon are all written as the
!     listing writes them.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! AND THE TWO CNOPs DO DIFFERENT THINGS, which is the alignment
! trap docs/NEXT.md recorded on jb_ax5b p.80 against p.82.
! Line 20's sits at 002464.40 and compiles a NOP, "000000.30 00",
! to reach the word boundary at 002465.00.  Line 27's sits at
! 002471.70 -- the no-zone row ends 56 bits into the word -- and
! compiles NOTHING, because there is no half word to put a NOP in;
! it rounds to 002472.00 and the listing prints neither a location
! nor a binary for it.  Same source line, two outcomes, both from
! the location counter.

        SLC, (8)2456.0

! ---- THE CHARACTER LOCATOR TABLES ---------------------------------
QFLD    ,0($2)                      ! line 4
        ,.6($2)                     ! line 5
        ,.12($2)                    ! line 6
        ,.18($2)                    ! line 7
        ,.24($2)                    ! line 8
        ,.30($2)                    ! line 9
        ,.36($2)                    ! line 10
        ,.42($2)                    ! line 11
        ,.48($2)                    ! line 12
        ,.54($2)                    ! line 13
        ,.60($2)                    ! line 14
        ,.66($2)                    ! line 15
        ,0.72($2)                   ! line 16 -- written with its
                                     !           word part, 0.72,
                                     !           where the twelve
                                     !           above are bare bit
                                     !           counts
! ---- THE TABLES ---------------------------------------------------
        CNOP                        ! line 20 -- compiles a NOP
Q       (AX)DD(BU,6,6),ABCDEFGHI+.)/X   ! line 21 -12 zone
        (AX)DD(BU,6,6),JKLMNOPQR-$*/X   ! line 22 -11 zone
        (AA)DD(BU,6,6),/STUVWXYZ0,(A    ! line 23 -zero zone, twelve
        DD(BU,6,6),(8)32                ! line 24 -SPECIAL FOR COLON
        (AX)DD(BU,6,6),123456789 =-/X   ! line 25 -no zone

        CNOP                        ! line 27 -- compiles nothing
QSAV    DRZ(BU,64),(6)              ! line 28

QTB     VF, 0                       ! line 30 -FOR 12 ZONE
        VF, 78                      ! line 31 -FOR THE 11 ZONE
        VF, 156                     ! line 32 -FOR THE ZERO ZONE
        VF, 234                     ! line 33 -FOR THE NO ZONE

        UNTAIL, (1)                 ! line 35 -- see note (2)

        END, QFLD

! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! AND TWO LISTING MARKS, the bare "*" after the location that every
! page since printed p.3 carries: lines 16 ("002464.00 *") and 28
! ("002472.00 *").
